{% doc %}
  Test-app fixture for config.approval_partial: lets an app answer the engine's
  question "must a proposed change wait for a person?" from its own state,
  instead of the operator editing MCP_CONFIG.

  INERT BY DEFAULT. With MCP_TEST_APPROVAL unset it returns nothing, and the
  engine falls back to config.approval_enforced — so every other suite sees the
  normal behaviour and this file changes nothing for them.

  MCP_TEST_APPROVAL:
    off          the gate is off for every tool
    on           the gate is on for every tool
    off:<tool>   the gate is off for that one tool and on for the rest. The
                 engine passes the tool being called, which is what makes a
                 per-tool answer possible; without it nothing here can match.
  Anything else returns nothing, which the engine must read as "no answer" and
  not as "do not enforce".

  The real use of this seam is an app whose own admins flip the gate in their own
  screens (pos-module-support does this from a desk setting).

  @param {string} [tool_name] - the tool being called, passed by queries/approval/enforced
{% enddoc %}
{% liquid
  assign mode = context.constants.MCP_TEST_APPROVAL | default: ''
  if mode == 'off'
    assign out = { "enforced": false }
    return out
  endif
  if mode == 'on'
    assign out = { "enforced": true }
    return out
  endif
  assign parts = mode | split: ':'
  if parts.first == 'off'
    assign named = parts[1]
    assign out = { "enforced": true }
    if named == tool_name
      assign out = { "enforced": false }
    endif
    return out
  endif
  return null
%}
